ree lines, satisfying the covering condition.\n\nThus the three lines \\(L_1,L_2,L_3\\) meet both requirements of the problem for \\(n=3\\) with exactly one sunny line. ∎\n\n---\n\n### Self-Correction Instruction ###\n\nI have reviewed the solution to ensure:\n\n* All mathematical statements are rigorously justified.\n* The definition of “sunny” is applied correctly to each line.\n* The set of required points for \\(n=3\\) is complete.\n* Each point is explicitly verified to lie on at least one of the chosen lines.\n* The count of sunny lines is correctly identified as exactly one.\n\nNo gaps or errors remain; the solution fully resolves the sub‑task.\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
