nny.  \nInstead keep \\(L_{2}=y=x\\) (covers (1,1) and (2,2)).  \nAdd a sunny line through (2,1) and (1,3): slope \\(-2\\). Equation: \\(y=-2x+5\\).  \n\nThus set  \n\n\\[\nL_{1}:x=1\\;(\\text{non‑sunny}),\\qquad\nL_{2}:y=x\\;(\\text{sunny}),\\qquad\nL_{3}:y=-2x+5\\;(\\text{sunny}).\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\nNow check:\n\n| \\((a,b)\\) | on \\(L_{1}\\)? | on \\(L_{2}\\)? | on \\(L_{3}\\)? | covered |\n|-----------|---------------|---------------|---------------|---------|\n| (1,1) | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | yes |\n| (1,2) | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | yes |\n| (2,1) | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ (since \\(-2\\cdot2+5=1\\)) | yes |\n| (1,3) | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ (since \\(-2\\cdot1+5=3\\)) | yes |\n| (3,1) | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | (3,1) is not on any of the three lines.  Need to cover (3,1).  \n\nAdd a sunny line through (3,1) and (2,2): slope \\(-1\\) (forbidden).  \nThrough (3,1) and (1,2): slope \\(-\\tfrac12\\) – sunny.  Equation: \\(y=-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac52\\).  \n\nReplace \\(L_{2}\\) by this line and keep \\(L_{3}=y=x\\).  \n\nFinal set:\n\n\\[\nL_{1}:x=1\\;(\\text{non‑sunny}),\\qquad\nL_{2}:y=-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac52\\;(\\text{sunny}),\\qquad\nL_{3}:y=x\\;(\\text{sunny}).\n\\tag{7}\n\\]\n\nNow the table:\n\n| \\((a,b)\\) | on \\(L_{1}\\)? | on \\(L_{2}\\)? | on \\(L_{3}\\)? | covered |\n|-----------|---------------|---------------|---------------|---------|\n| (1,1) | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | yes |\n| (1,2) | ✓ | ✓ (since \\(-\\tfrac12\\cdot1+ \\tfrac52 =2\\)) | ✗ | yes |\n| (2,1) | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | (2,1) not covered – still a problem.  \n\nWe need a systematic construction; the earlier attempt with \\(k=2\\) was flawed.  \n\nA correct construction for \\(k=2\\) is:\n\n\\[\nL_{1}:x=1\\;(\\text{non‑sunny}),\\qquad\nL_{2}:y= x\\;(\\text{sunny}),\\qquad\nL_{3}:y=-\\tfrac12x+\\tfrac52\\;(\\text{sunny}).\n\\tag{8}\n\\]\n\nCheck again:\n\n- (1,1): on \\(L_{1}\\) and \\(L_{2}\\).\n- (1,2): on \\(L_{1}\\) and \\(L_{3}\\) (since \\(-\\tfrac12\\cdot1+ \\tfrac52 =2\\)).\n- (2,1): not on \\(L_{1}\\); on \\(L_{2}\\)? No (since \\(2\\neq1\\)); on \\(L_{3}\\)? \\(-\\tfr